# PRD Workspace Architecture

## Layout (relative to the workspace root)

```
prds/<feature-slug>.md                         one PRD per feature
stories/<feature-slug>-<NN>-<story-slug>.md    one story per file
research/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<source>.md              raw input, never spec
decisions/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md               settled trade-offs
docs/                                          command output (validation, tickets, status)
glossary.md                                    domain terms, alphabetical
scripts/check_prd.py                           structure checker
.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc                       lint config
```

## One PRD per file

- File name is the feature slug: `prds/budget-alerts.md`.
- One H1 per PRD: `# PRD: <Feature name>`.
- A PRD covers one feature. Two features means two PRDs.
- Required H2 headings, in this order: Problem, Goals, Non-goals, Users, Epics, User Stories, Non-functional Requirements, Edge Cases, Dependencies, Rollout Plan, Success Metrics, Open Questions.
- Required H3 under Non-functional Requirements: Performance, Security, Privacy, Accessibility, Internationalization, Observability.

## One story per file

- Name: `stories/<feature-slug>-<NN>-<story-slug>.md`. `NN` is two digits, never reused.
- Story ID: a 2 to 4 letter feature prefix plus `NN`, for example `BA-03`.
- H1: `# <ID>: <short title>`.
- Header lines directly under the H1: `**Epic:** E<n> ...`, `**Goal:** G<n>`, `**Size:** S|M|L`.
- Sections: Story, Acceptance Criteria, Edge Cases, INVEST Check.
- The PRD's User Stories section is an index table that links to each file. Story text lives only in the story file.

## IDs

| Thing | Format | Defined in |
|---|---|---|
| Goal | `G1`, `G2` | PRD `## Goals` |
| Epic | `E1`, `E2` | PRD `## Epics` table |
| Story | `BA-01` | `stories/` file H1 |
| NFR | `NFR-PERF-1` | PRD `## Non-functional Requirements` |
| Decision | file date + slug | `decisions/` |

IDs are permanent. A dropped story keeps its ID and moves to a "Dropped" row in the index.

## Glossary

- `glossary.md` holds one H2 per term, alphabetical, with a one-line definition.
- The first use of a glossary term in a PRD is linked: `[safe-to-spend](../glossary.md#safe-to-spend)`.

## Links

- Use relative links only. `../stories/budget-alerts-01-set-category-limit.md`, never absolute paths.
- No links to private tools inside story text. Put tracker links in the PRD index only.
